n": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 6, 12]], "date-time": "2026-06-12T15:18:06Z", "timestamp": 1781277486000}, "score": 32.944912, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.techrxiv.org/doi/full/10.36227/techrxiv.174612962.26131807/v1"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025, 5, 1]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.174612962.26131807/v1", "relation": {"has-version": [{"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.36227/techrxiv.174612962.26131807/v4", "asserted-by": "object"}, {"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.36227/techrxiv.174612962.26131807/v3", "asserted-by": "object"}, {"id-type": "doi", "id": "10.36227/techrxiv.174612962.26131807/v2", "asserted-by": "object"}]}, "published": {"date-parts": [[2025, 5, 1]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 28]], "date-time": "2026-08-28T05:29:32Z", "timestamp": 1787894972872, "version": "build-2784847793"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 2]]}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers (IEEE)", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 2]], "date-time": "2025-06-02T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1748822400000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>\n                  Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) have sparked growing interest in building fully autonomous agents. However, fully autonomous LLM-based agents still face significant challenges, including limited reliability due to hallucinations, difficulty in handling complex tasks, and substantial safety and ethical risks, all of which limit their feasibility and trustworthiness in real-world applications. To overcome these limitations, LLM-based human-agent systems (LLM-HAS) incorporate human-provided information, feedback, or control into the agent system to enhance system performance, reliability and safety. This paper provides the first comprehensive and structured survey of LLM-HAS. It clarifies fundamental concepts, systematically presents core components shaping these systems, including environment &amp; profiling, human feedback, interaction types, orchestration and communication, explores emerging applications, and discusses unique challenges and opportunities. By consolidating current knowledge and offering a structured overview, we aim to foster further research and innovation in this rapidly evolving interdisciplinary field. Paper lists and resources are available at GitHub repository:\u00a0\n                  <jats:ext-link xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"https://github.com/HenryPengZou/Awesome-LLM-Based-Human-Agent-Systems\">https://github.com/HenryPengZou/Awesome-LLM-Based-Human-Agent-Systems</jats:ext-link>\n                </jats:p>", "DOI": "10.36227/techrxiv.174612962.26131807/v2", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 2]], "date-time": "2025-06-02T14:34:16Z", "timestamp": 1748874856000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 2, "title": ["A Survey on Large Language Model based Human-Agent Systems"], "prefix": "10.36227", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5259-4998", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Henry Peng", "family": "Zou", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Illinois Chicago"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Wei-Chieh", "family": "Huang", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Illinois Chicago"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yaozu", "family": "Wu", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "The University of Tokyo"}], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Yankai", "family": "Chen", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "University of Illinois Chicago"}], "role": [{"voc